\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Estimated Conditional Probability versus True Conditional Probability in Study 2. Each data point is a pair of two questions. The red line represents the optimal prediction while the dark line represents the fit of the linear models. Panel A shows all trials combined, panel B shows trials in the Fast condition (20-second time limit), and panel C shows trials in the Slow condition (40-second time limit). Points are colored by the difficulty difference between the evaluated and observed questions.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:S2-fig-behav}{{3}{5}{Estimated Conditional Probability versus True Conditional Probability in Study 2. Each data point is a pair of two questions. The red line represents the optimal prediction while the dark line represents the fit of the linear models. Panel A shows all trials combined, panel B shows trials in the Fast condition (20-second time limit), and panel C shows trials in the Slow condition (40-second time limit). Points are colored by the difficulty difference between the evaluated and observed questions}{figure.3}{}}
